    ShowMainForm: bool
    '''
    Determines whether the application shows its main form on startup.

    Use ``ShowMainForm`` to control whether and when the application shows its main form.

    The default value of ``True`` is set in the constructor. When ``ShowMainForm`` is ``True``, the main window shows automatically when the application starts. The ``MainForm`` property specifies which form is the main form. To hide the main form at startup, set ``ShowMainForm`` to ``False`` in the main project file before the call to the ``Run()`` method. Make sure that the ``Visible`` property of the ``Form`` is also false.
    '''
    Terminated: bool
