class Collection(Persistent):
    '''
    ==========================
    System.Classes.TCollection
    ==========================

    ``Collection`` is a container for `CollectionItem <System.Classes.TCollectionItem.htm>`__ objects.

    Each ``Collection`` holds a group of `CollectionItem <System.Classes.TCollectionItem.htm>`__ descendants. ``Collection`` maintains an index of the collection items in its `Items <System.Classes.TCollection.Items.htm>`__ array. The `Count <System.Classes.TCollection.Count.htm>`__ property contains the number of items in the collection. Use the `Add <System.Classes.TCollection.Add.htm>`__ and `Delete <System.Classes.TCollection.Delete.htm>`__ methods to add items to the collection and delete items from the collection.

    Objects descended from ``Collection`` can contain objects descended from `CollectionItem <System.Classes.TCollectionItem.htm>`__. Thus, for each ``Collection`` descendant, there is a corresponding `CollectionItem <System.Classes.TCollectionItem.htm>`__ descendant.

    The following table lists some typical descendants of ``Collection`` with the corresponding `CollectionItem <System.Classes.TCollectionItem.htm>`__ descendant and the component that uses each pair:

    ================================================================================ ======================================================================== ===================================================================================
    **Collection Descendant**                                                        **CollectionItem Descendant**                                            **Component**
