    ImeMode: ImeMode
    '''
    Determines the behavior of the *Input Method Editor* (IME).

    Set `ImeMode <Vcl.Controls.TWinControl.ImeMode.htm>`__ to configure the way an *IME* processes user keystrokes. An *IME* is a front-end input processor for Asian language characters. The *IME* hooks all keyboard input, converts it to Asian characters in a conversion window, and sends the converted characters or strings on to the application.

    `ImeMode <Vcl.Controls.TWinControl.ImeMode.htm>`__ allows a control to influence the type of conversion performed by the *IME* so that it is appropriate for the input expected by the control. For example, a control that only accepts numeric input might specify an `ImeMode <Vcl.Controls.TWinControl.ImeMode.htm>`__ of ``imClose``, as no conversion is necessary for numeric input.

