    Set `FixedColor <Vcl.Grids.TCustomGrid.FixedColor.htm>`__ to specify the color for the nonscrolling cells in the grid. The scrolling region of the grid is drawn using the ``Color`` property.
    '''
    FixedCols: int
    '''
    Specifies the number of columns on the left of the grid that cannot be scrolled.

    Set `FixedCols <Vcl.Grids.TCustomGrid.FixedCols.htm>`__ to create or get rid of nonscrolling columns. Nonscrolling columns appear at the left of the grid, and are always visible, even when the user scrolls the other columns in the grid. Use nonscrolling columns for displaying row titles or row numbers, or to implement a scroll lock that the user can set.

