        When the `Customizable <Vcl.ComCtrls.TToolBar.Customizable.htm>`__ property is ``True``, the user can add buttons to the ``ToolBar`` using the ``ToolBar`` customize dialog. ``OnCustomizeCanInsert`` occurs when the user tries to add a ``Button``, and allows the application to reject the insertion. If the ``OnCustomizeCanInsert`` event handler sets its ``Allow`` parameter to ``False``, the ``ToolBar`` customize dialog rejects the insertion.

        OnCustomizeCanInsert is an event handler of type `Vcl.ComCtrls.TTBCustomizeQueryEvent <Vcl.ComCtrls.TTBCustomizeQueryEvent.htm>`__.
